  "localized_copy": [
    {
      "locale": "en",
      "node_id": "world02_mission_011_node_001",
      "fields": {
        "level_label": "LEVEL 11:",
        "title": "The Daily Habit Loop",
        "key_label": "KEY ACQUIRED:",
        "key_acquired": "DISCIPLINE & AUTOMATION",
        "objective_label": "MISSION OBJECTIVE",
        "objective": "Learning why 'Automating' your boring habits saves your brain's battery for the fun stuff.",
        "status_label": "LOADING MAP ASSETS... [COMPLETED]"
      }
    },
    {
      "locale": "en",
      "node_id": "world02_mission_011_node_002",
      "fields": {
        "story_heading": "THE DAILY HABIT LOOP",
        "log_label": "SYSTEM LOG >>",
        "text": "20:15. The Bathroom of Doom. Dilo stood by the sink, staring at his toothbrush like it was a live grenade. He was casually juggling a half-empty tube of toothpaste with his feet, showing off his soccer skills. Nini, the tiny burst of joy, was trying to squeeze 'Sparkle Paste' onto her brush, doing a perfect spin at the same time, but it exploded like a glittery volcano, splashing onto the mirror."
      }
    },
    {
      "locale": "en",
      "node_id": "world02_mission_011_node_003",
      "fields": {
        "speaker_label": "NINI",
        "text": "Oops! I made modern art! The mirror looks pretty now! Maybe the bacteria will see how pretty it is and decide to be friendly and leave our teeth on their own?"
      }
    },
    {
      "locale": "en",
      "node_id": "world02_mission_011_node_004",
      "fields": {
        "speaker_label": "LULI",
        "text": "(Hanging upside down from her gymnastic ribbons in the hallway, reading a science book) Bacteria don't have feelings, Nini. They don't care about art. They just have a giant appetite for sugar."
      }
    },
    {
      "locale": "en",
      "node_id": "world02_mission_011_node_005",
      "fields": {
        "speaker_label": "DILO",
        "text": "Well, I want to eat sugar too, but I don't poop on people's teeth! Seriously, I brushed them yesterday! And I put my shoes away! And I packed my backpack! Why is real life just repeating the same boring side quests over and over?! Can't I just eat a mint and call it a win?"
      }
    },
    {
      "locale": "en",
      "node_id": "world02_mission_011_node_006",
      "fields": {
        "log_label": "SYSTEM LOG >>",
        "text": "Mimi, the Brain Captain, leaned against the doorframe. She looked incredibly tired. The \"I've answered 400 questions today\" kind of tired. She closed her eyes, placing her hand on her chest. She took a slow, deep breath in for 4 seconds, held it, and blew it out for 8 seconds."
      }
    },
    {
      "locale": "en",
      "node_id": "world02_mission_011_node_007",
      "fields": {
        "speaker_label": "MIMI",
        "text": "Captain needs a deep calm-down breath. My Lizard brain is waking up, and it wants to yell about the sparkly mirror. (She opens her eyes, looking patient again, holding a laundry basket like a shield.) Dilo, we talked about this. Doing things you don't want to do isn't a punishment; it's a cheat code to save your battery."
      }
    },
    {
      "locale": "en",
      "node_id": "world02_mission_011_node_008",
      "fields": {
        "speaker_label": "DILO",
        "text": "It doesn't feel like a cheat code. It feels like playing a game for zero points. Every morning it's \"brush, dress, pack.\" Every night it's \"brush, pajamas, sleep.\" It's a never-ending cleaning loop! I am trapped!"
      }
    },
    {
      "locale": "en",
      "node_id": "world02_mission_011_node_009",
      "fields": {
        "log_label": "SYSTEM LOG >>",
        "text": "Alio ran in, wearing his signature safety helmet and holding a toilet brush like a sword. Behind him, he had already built a Level 4 wall in the hallway using laundry baskets, towels, and carefully stacked toilet paper rolls. He looked frantic, searching the ceiling for threats."
      }
    },
    {
      "locale": "en",
      "node_id": "world02_mission_011_node_010",
      "fields": {
        "speaker_label": "ALIO",
        "text": "A time loop?! Are we trapped?! Dilo said if you don't brush, creepy cave spiders spin webs in your mouth while you sleep and lay eggs in your gums! Is that true?! Mammi, get the vacuum! I built a strong fort, but I don't know if it will hold against mouth-spiders!"
      }
    },
    {
      "locale": "en",
      "node_id": "world02_mission_011_node_011",
      "fields": {
        "speaker_label": "LULI",
        "text": "(Dropping gracefully from the ribbons, landing like a ninja, and tapping her clipboard with a pen) No spiders, Alio. Just bacteria poop. That's what plaque is. Bacteria eating sugar and pooping acid on your enamel. Also, Dilo, your logic is totally broken. You don't complain about having to charge your phone every single day, do you?"
      }
    },
    {
      "locale": "en",
      "node_id": "world02_mission_011_node_012",
      "fields": {
        "speaker_label": "DILO",
        "text": "That's different! My phone gives me joy! This toothbrush just tastes like spicy chalk!"
      }
    },
    {
      "locale": "en",
      "node_id": "world02_mission_011_node_013",
      "fields": {
        "speaker_label": "MIMI",
        "text": "Listen to me, crew. Every time you argue with yourself about whether you should do a chore, you are burning your Brain Battery. Deciding takes 10% of your energy. Arguing with me takes 20%. And it drains my battery too. But if you just Automate it - if you do it without thinking, in the exact same order every day like a robot - it only takes 1% of your battery."
      }
    },
    {
      "locale": "en",
      "node_id": "world02_mission_011_node_014",
      "fields": {
        "speaker_label": "ALIO",
        "text": "Like... a robot? I want to be a Cyborg! Beep boop. Turning on anti-poop lasers. Destroying bacteria. Starting the upgrade to my back teeth!"
      }
    },
    {
      "locale": "en",
      "node_id": "world02_mission_011_node_015",
      "fields": {
        "speaker_label": "MIMI",
        "text": "Exactly like a robot. You put on pajamas, you grab the brush, you hit play on the Battle Music. You don't think, you just do the steps. The faster you automate the boring stuff, the more brainpower you save for Minecraft, soccer, and reading. We are a team, and the team needs everyone's shields up."
      }
    },
    {
      "locale": "en",
      "node_id": "world02_mission_011_node_016",
      "fields": {
        "speaker_label": "DILO",
        "text": "Fine. But I'm playing the Boss Fight music. If I have to fight tiny invaders, I need epic music."
      }
    },
    {
      "locale": "en",
      "node_id": "world02_mission_011_node_017",
      "fields": {
        "log_label": "SYSTEM LOG >>",
        "text": "Dilo tapped his phone. Heavy electronic boss-battle music blasted so loud the toothbrushes shook in their cups. Alio started brushing so fast his helmet shook, looking like a human blender. Nini hugged Mimi's leg, leaving a massive smear of pink sparkle paste on her jeans, swaying her hips to the heavy beat."
      }
    },
    {
      "locale": "en",
      "node_id": "world02_mission_011_node_018",
      "fields": {
        "speaker_label": "NINI",
        "text": "I automated, Mammi! My teeth are sparkling like a disco ball! Are my shields up?"
      }
    },
    {
      "locale": "en",
      "node_id": "world02_mission_011_node_019",
